Option A(i) lid pack, hinge harness, mass and stability, base pockets: v2/cad/lid_pack_a1.py (MESHSAT-1357, stream a1mech, 29 Sep 2026)
Prototype design, AI review: nothing built, bought or fitted. Analytical success is not physical verification or fabrication readiness.

1. THE LID, at Peli's figures
   face top Z 106.52 nominal (104.77 to 108.27), ceiling Z 154.44 nominal (152.66 at the worst: rim 108.97 - 0.76 + web lid 44.45)
   room face top to ceiling: 47.92 nominal, 44.39 worst, 42.11 with every unstated allowance taken twice (frame_seat.out M3; r2 record B)
   flat ceiling 346.16 x 231.86 (STEP #736); fillets R 16.26 to the walls, then an R 1.27 step; lid cavity 373.88 x 261.87 at the parting plane
   ribs in the lid cavity: 0 (the top STEP's cavity faces are the drafted walls, the fillets, the R 1.27 step and the ceiling)
   gasket land: the lid's seal seats on the base's tongue outboard of the cavity (X 195.56..201.96, CASE-MARGINS 2.3); every lid item here
   stays inboard of the cavity walls, so none bears on the seal; the fillet's depth below the ceiling at 2, 5, 8, 12 mm outboard of the
   flat edge: 0.12, 0.79, 2.10, 5.29
   plan allowance between a lid item and a face part: 1.06 (lid place 0.76 + bonded plate 0.30, INFERRED); minimum clearance 1.0

