2. THE LID MODULE
   cell: Samsung INR18650-35E, d 18.55 max, L 65.25 max, 50 g max (spec Ver. 1.1, 3.10 and the drawing); 3.35 Ah min, 3.60 V
   block: A06's construction (the ruled base block's): cells touching at 18.55, wrap 0.5 a side, 1.0 at each end joint along the axis;
   cells lie with their axis along X, three or four end to end (series joints at the end gaps), one layer across Y, and a second layer
   nested in the grooves of the first, 16.065 further from the ceiling (toward the face), wherever the face under it allows
   stack from the ceiling: bond 0.20 + 5052-H32 plate 2.00 + block (19.55 one layer, 35.61 two) + PORON pad 1.00 + cover 1.25
   module depth: one layer 24.00, two layers 40.06; own allowances {'bond': 0.1, 'plate': 0.13, 'standoff': 0.1, 'cover': 0.1} = 0.43 (INFERRED, none stated by a source)
   P2 (ASSUMPTION until fnd/a1elec reports): board P's outline 70 x 44, tallest part 16.17 (Keystone 3568 with its blade, packfit_west.out),
   on 3.0 standoffs: depth 22.97, inside the one-layer depth
   venting: the maker's sheet names venting as a failure outcome (8.1.2) and states no clearance; every cell end faces its 1.0 joint, the
   cover's X-end bays are open slots, so gas from a cell is not sealed in the module: it enters the closed case, which Peli's pressure valve
   relieves (ruling 7 Sep 2026 00:52). Heat: the sheet asks the pack away from heat sources (page 17); the lid is away from the PA and CM5s.

