   RETENTION of the module (arrangement B, every place filled: 56 cells), to the r2 set's load case: 100 g in each direction
     module 3.46 kg (cells at 50 g max, the rest ESTIMATE): 3390 N at 100 g. Bond area under the lid plate about 46502 mm2 (the slices and bays):
     mean stress 0.073 MPa in tension (a drop on the base pulls the module off the ceiling) or shear (on an end). DP8005's sheet gives no
     strength on polypropylene (its 0.3 MPa is the overlap shear at which a part may be handled, a cure milestone, not a rating) and no
     peel figure but T-peel on 0.5 mm HDPE: the bond is bounded by no held figure, OPEN at T8 (a pull test of a bonded plate on Peli's
     polypropylene after a thermal cycle) and E1 with an accelerometer on the lid, as the r2 set's bond is.
     the block to the plate: cell glue between cells and a fillet to the plate (adhesive TBD): 49 N per cell at 100 g (0.8 N/mm on a
     cell's 65.25 mm contact line); the cover on eight M3 standoffs in the end bays catches the block if the glue lets go: 343 N each
     at 100 g, against the r2 record's 1019 N for a button head on a 3.0 printed part (a 1.0 cover takes less; the cover's spans of
     65 to 200 between bays are not a beam that carries the block: the glue is the primary hold, the cover a catch). OPEN at E1.
     Peli states no load for its hinges or the lid's stop; the lid grows from about 1.4 (shell and QMX set) to 4.9 kg: T-A1-4 (and the
     lid stay, section 4).
     heater: the lid pack's own mat (9h: the charge window starts at 0 C) is not placed; a 1.0 mat between the plate and the block
     deepens both depths by 1.0: the tightest rows (the window 3.10, the LED bar 2.40 at the worst) still meet 1.0.

3. THE HINGE HARNESS (the lid pack to the base), for arrangement B
   current (ASSUMPTION for fnd/a1elec): 10 A continuous, 18 A for 60 s with the base pack isolated, 8.6 A of charge
   conductor: 12 AWG fine-strand silicone, 5.21 mOhm/m (annealed copper), OD 4.4 (INFERRED class); run 0.45 m in the lid + 0.35 m in the base;
   loop 8.34 mOhm: at 10 A 83 mV and 0.83 W; at 18 A 150 mV and 2.70 W; adiabatic rise over 60 s at 18 A: 8.9 K (copper 3.31 mm2, 385 J/kgK)
   hinge axis (ESTIMATE, no Peli figure): Y 155.0 +-8.0, Z 111.0 +-5.0; lid tie T_L (128.0, 111.5) on the lid's inner back wall; plate tie T_P (122.0, 106.52)
   T_L and T_P are 150 apart in X, so the lead between them runs along the back channel and the lid's travel moves one end sideways
   opening   T_L (Y, Z)            Y-Z offset T_L..T_P   chord T_L..T_P
