   T_L turns at R 27.0 about the axis. Lead between the ties: 169.7 (the longest chord, 161.6 at 180 degrees, plus 5 percent).
   Closed, the lead bows 33.1 (in the X-Z plane of the back channel, which is about 14 wide in Y and 40 tall), radius about 102; fully
   open it is an S across an offset of 60.1 over 150, radius about 94. Requirement on the pick (INFERRED class): a flexing radius of
   10 x OD = 44 or less, met by both figures above: yes.
   route (B): from P2 (X -134..-90, Y -73..-3) through the module's west bay (X -141..-134) north to the back channel (Y 114.93 to the lid's
   back wall, about 130.9 at the parting plane), east along it on bonded tie mounts to T_L at X -121, then the free lead to T_P at X 29 on
   the plate's full-thickness face near its back edge (Y 122), then to the crossing. About 0.45 m in the lid, as assumed above.
   strain relief: a bonded tie mount at T_L and at T_P and every 60 mm or less along both runs (the r2 set's tie-mount rule), and a
   printed guide on the lid's back wall that keeps the free lead inboard of the cavity wall (Y < 130.9) so that closing folds it toward
   the face and never over the rim or the seal.
   disconnect: at the lid side beside P2, an XT60 pair (Amass XT60, the tree's pack connector, v2/vendor/battery/amass-xt60-spec-tme.pdf)
   and a JST XH 1x4 for SMBus, so that the lid comes off its hinge as ASSEMBLY.md section 7 has it; fused at P2 (the string fuse of 8a's class).
   crossing the sealed face: NOT designed; it is S-95's crossing (EQ-31), which the QMX leads already need. This harness adds to it: two
   power poles of 25 A or more and four signal contacts, sealed mated and unmated, on the plate's back band or at a site outside every
   lid item's plan; on the plate it must clear the frame's ring, the backer's top strip and B16's tall parts. Until it is designed, the
   lid pack cannot be connected with the lid closed and sealed.
   the QMX's DC lead (r2: looped back at R 20 WEST of the tray) is re-routed EAST because the pack now lies west of the tray: (106.3, -37.5) -> (106.3, -92.9) -> (126.3, -112.9) -> (158.0, -112.9) -> (178.0, -92.9) -> (178.0, 100.0)

