   verdict (B): the open case stands on level ground up to a lid opening of 120 degrees in every swept case; beyond it a light base with
   its CG back and high tips on level ground (first at 135 degrees swept). Fix, the session's (authority SESSION, reversible): a lid stay
   that stops the lid at 100 degrees (a webbing strap between two bonded anchors, one on the lid's inner back wall, one on the face
   plate's rebated back band; no hole in the case or the plate; about EUR 10, ESTIMATE; it folds into the back channel when the lid
   closes), which also carries the lid's added mass off Peli's hinge stop. With it the
   worst back slope the open case stands on is 10.0 deg (B) and 12.5 deg (A); the operator's sheet states: open the lid only on ground
   sloping less than 9 degrees toward the hinge side. If Peli's own stop is at or under 100 degrees the stay is not needed for
   stability; the stop angle and the hinge axis are read on the mock-up (T-A1-3).

